| Topic | Details |
|-------|---------|
| **Location** | Place de l’Étoile, 75008 Paris, France |
| **Coordinates** | 48.8738 ° N, 2.2950 ° E |
| **Height** | 50 m (164 ft) |
| **Width** | 45 m (148 ft) |
| **Construction** | • Designed by Jean Chalgrin<br>• Built 1806‑1836 (post‑Napoleon)<br>• 12 arches (one for each major French army) |
| **Key Features** | • **Tomb of the Unknown Soldier** (bronze cenotaph, 1921)<br>• **Rotating flame** lit daily at 8 pm<br>• **Victory Column** (35 m tall, 12 m wide, 4 m thick)<br>• 360° panoramic view from the top |
